From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] Make the GTK4 Activity Share control visible and named

GTK4 ShareButton inherited RadioMenuButton without an icon or tooltip.  The
button consequently had an empty accessible name and could collapse to zero
width in ActivityToolbar, leaving the working share action undiscoverable.
Use the existing neighborhood icon and expose the stable Sugar label while
keeping the radio palette and sharing behavior unchanged.

--- a/src/sugar4/activity/widgets.py
+++ b/src/sugar4/activity/widgets.py
@@ -183,1 +183,6 @@
-        RadioMenuButton.__init__(self, **kwargs)
+        kwargs.setdefault("icon_name", "zoom-neighborhood")
+        kwargs.setdefault("tooltip", _("Share"))
+        RadioMenuButton.__init__(self, **kwargs)
+        # RadioMenuButton consumes the tooltip for its palette, while the
+        # ToolButton label is also needed by GTK4 accessibility.
+        self.set_tooltip(_("Share"))
